    <statement><p>If <m>g(1)=1,</m> <m>g(5)=-5,</m> and <m>\displaystyle \int_1^5 \! g(x) \, dx = -10,</m> evaluate the integral <m>\displaystyle \int_1^5 \! x g'(x)\, dx.</m></p>
<p>Answer: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5\cdot \left(-5\right)-1--10</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>SOLUTION</p>
<p>Let <m>u = x, \; dv = g'(x) \, dx \; \Rightarrow \; du = dx, \; v = g(x).</m> We then have
<me>\int_1^5 \! x g'(x)\, dx  = \Big[x g(x)\Big]_1^5 - \int_1^5 g(x) \, dx 
= \Big[ 5\cdot g(5) - 1 \cdot g(1) \Big]  + 10 
=  5\cdot (-5) - 1  + 10  = -16</me></p>
</solution>
